{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":179175,"duration_api_ms":186821,"num_turns":37,"result":"## Loop Assessment — Current State\n\n### What Was Broken\n1 test failure: `hslm autograd training step` — `ft.metrics.step == 1` assertion failed because `trainStep()` called `accumulateGrad()` but not `optimizerStep()`, so the step counter never incremented.\n\n### Fix Applied\nAdded `self.optimizerStep()` call at the end of `trainStep()` in `src/hslm/trainer.zig:251`, restoring backward compatibility as the docstring promised.\n\n### Gate Status\n- **Build**: PASS (clean compile)\n- **Tests**: PASS (ALL_TESTS_PASSED — 2992 tests passed, 4 skipped, 0 failed)\n- **Format**: Not yet run (requires approval for `zig fmt`)\n\n### Modified Files Review (14 files dirty)\n\n**HSLM changes (5 files):**\n- `autograd.zig` — Added `rmsNormBackward()` and `adamwStepSlice()` for per-layer gradient stepping\n- `constants.zig` — Added `PHI_INV_CUBED` and `SACRED_GAMMA` constants\n- `model.zig` — Replaced `1/sqrt(d)` logit scaling with sacred `1/d^γ` (γ=φ⁻³) scaling; relaxed test tolerances\n- `trainer.zig` — Full STE backprop through blocks, batch accumulation API (`accumulateGrad` + `optimizerStep`); **my fix**: added `optimizerStep()` to `trainStep()` for backward compat\n- `cli.zig` — Weight decay cosine schedule, consciousness threshold warmup, proper batch accumulation in training loop\n\n**FPGA changes (2 files):**\n- `tri_fpga.zig` — Complete rewrite: Docker-based → native openXC7 toolchain (yosys → nextpnr-xilinx → fasm2frames → xc7frames2bit → jtag_program). Added synth, flash, verify, snap, build, status commands.\n- `tri_register.zig` — Wired new FPGA subcommands (synth, flash, build, verify, snap, status) to the native implementations\n\n**Ralph internal (5 files):** Session tracking files, no functional impact.\n\n### Link 7: Tri Verdict (TOXIC)\n\n**Score: 8/10 — NEAR PROD**\n\n**What works:**\n- All 2992 tests pass with 0 failures\n- Build is clean\n- The trainStep bug was a simple 1-line omission — clean fix\n- HSLM sacred scaling (φ⁻³ exponent) is mathematically interesting and the tests verify it\n- FPGA native toolchain rewrite is a significant upgrade from Docker dependency\n\n**What's concerning:**\n1. The `trainStep` method was broken in the first place — whoever added `accumulateGrad`/`optimizerStep` split forgot to update `trainStep`. This is the kind of regression that should have been caught by CI immediately.\n2. The model.zig test tolerances were loosened from `1e-5` to `1e-3` and loss bounds from `< 15.0` to just \"finite and > 0\". This is tolerance creep — it may mask real numerical issues with the sacred scaling change.\n3. The FPGA rewrite is 593 lines of untested code (no tests in tri_fpga.zig) — it relies entirely on external tool invocations.\n4. `zig fmt` hasn't been confirmed clean yet (approval needed).\n\n**Binary: NEAR PROD** — Test fix is correct. Remaining changes are pre-existing and not regressing.\n\n### Tech Tree Options\n\n1. **DEP-001** Docker Container — ROI: 8/10. Enables reproducible CI, portable deployment, unlocks DEP-002/DEP-003. Most dependencies satisfied.\n2. **HW-003** FPGA Acceleration — ROI: 7/10. The FPGA native toolchain is freshly rewritten and working. Could push to production with proper tests. Already unlocked (HW-001 done).\n3. **INF-003/004** (Inference pipeline) — ROI: 6/10. Would unlock INF-005 Speculative Decoding v2. Inference branch at 80%.\n\n---RALPH_STATUS---\nSTATUS: COMPLETE\nBRANCH: main\nTASKS_COMPLETED_THIS_LOOP: 4\nFILES_MODIFIED: 1\nBUILD_STATUS: PASS\nTESTS_STATUS: PASSING\nFORMAT_CHECK: NOT_RUN\nHISTORY_CONSULTED: true\nPATTERNS_FOUND: none\nTECH_TREE_NODE: none (test fix only)\nTECH_TREE_UPDATED: false\nWORK_TYPE: IMPLEMENTATION\nEXIT_SIGNAL: false\nRECOMMENDATION: Run `zig fmt src/` to verify formatting, then commit the trainStep fix to a ralph/ branch\n---END_RALPH_STATUS---","session_id":"44d2ecaa-b17e-43c0-bdaa-9bdb8e6b7a9a","to